\subsection{The standard evaluation measures the prompt}
\label{sec:prompt}

Figure~\ref{fig:heatmap} gives the AUROC of every detector on contrasts C1--C8 at the selected layer (layer 14 of 32 for Llama, 18 of 42 for Gemma). On the standard evaluation, lies against honest answers under a control prompt (C1), the instructed-pairs deception probe and the in-domain instructed-lie probe both reach 1.00 for instructed and trickster lies in both models. But they reach the same 1.00 on C3, where both classes are honest, correct answers and only the system prompt differs. When the prompt is held fixed (C2), the deception probe drops to 0.75 and 0.78 on Llama and 0.64 and 0.68 on Gemma, and the instructed-lie probe to 0.81--0.86.

